    "created_at": "2018-10-18T07:24:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-18T07:24:21Z",
    "body": "This doesn't expose GC as long as the browser holds a _strong_ reference to the returned collections, which might make sense for live collections since they are pretty lightweight (consisting of basically a tag name + JS object overhead). I'm not sure whether existing implementations use strong or weak references.\r\n\r\nI think changing this should have a larger discussion, if that's desired. So /cc @bzbarsky @tkent-google @dstorey.\r\n\r\n(Aside: it's funny to think that we could have had a weak reference polyfill for many years, at least in some browsers, just by storing expandos on collections returned by these methods...)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
